# 2.1.4 WP9 line W1 (plan section 8, D14): the Wi-Fi driver's speed-optimised code moves from IRAM to flash.
#
# STAGED, OFF BY DEFAULT: no build reads this file unless it names it, so CP7's image is unchanged.
# Built only as a G-M variant, in a build folder and with an sdkconfig of its own (README.md here):
#   idf.py -B <folder> -D SDKCONFIG=<folder>\sdkconfig.wp9
#          -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.wp9/w1_wifi_iram_off.defaults" build
# Never put these lines in the project's sdkconfig. After the gate passes they move to
# sdkconfig.defaults with an I14 guard in main/main.c (README.md has the guard).
#
# Frees: with ESP_WIFI_IRAM_OPT off, libpp's and libnet80211's .wifi0iram sections, libcoexist's
#   .coexiram and three esp_wifi functions (7,275 B); with ESP_WIFI_RX_IRAM_OPT off, .wifirxiram and
#   .wifislprxiram (10,305 B; the second moves because ESP_WIFI_SLP_IRAM_OPT is off too). On the
#   ESP32-S3 the DIRAM this code leaves becomes internal, DMA-capable heap.
# Estimate: 17,580 B, summed from CP5's map (its IRAM input sections; DIRAM .text is unchanged since):
#   DIRAM .text 113,387 -> about 95,800 B, heap about +17.5 KB, flash .text about +17.6 KB.
#   Not the "+27 KB or more" of plan section 8: that is the Kconfig help's figure for every such
#   function, and only the ones this image links move.
# Gate (G-M): the IRAM gate re-baselined (record the new DIRAM .text; I10's 113,387 B no longer
#   applies); G-CNA P-1 to P-6, each step's p90 within +20 % of CP7's (P-5, the page load, above
#   all), S1 and S2, an iPhone and an Android phone, 10 runs each; TLS and DPS regression (connect
#   times within +20 %, no esp-tls or mbedTLS error); LS-1's leak -> CLOSE within 200 ms unchanged;
#   adverts per burst within +-5 % (coexistence code moves too). Fallback if the page gate fails:
#   ESP_WIFI_IRAM_OPT off alone (7,275 B), built from this file with only that symbol deleted
#   (README.md).
# Verified in ESP-IDF 5.5.1: both are bool options with no dependency in components/esp_wifi/Kconfig
#   (lines 274 and 292; default y on this target); esp_wifi/linker.lf and esp_coex/linker.lf map the
#   sections; wifi_init.c's boot lines "WiFi IRAM OP enabled" and "WiFi RX IRAM OP enabled" go.
#   kconfgen gives no warning, and the deprecated aliases ESP32_WIFI_(RX_)IRAM_OPT follow.
# CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_IRAM_OPT is not set
# CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_RX_IRAM_OPT is not set
